  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The figure below shows a block of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>, kept on a rough inclined plane of angle&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>°</mo></math>&nbsp;and coefficient of static friction equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>.&nbsp;It is being acted upon by two forces. What should be the minimum&nbsp;value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;(in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>) so that the block doesn't slip downwards? <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo></math>Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>]</mo></math></p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0059_f42222e82706.png\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 122px;\" /></p>\r"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "16.25",
  "solution": {
